# Line endings are pinned on purpose.
#
# Everything is stored and checked out with LF. Two test fixtures are the
# exception and must keep their bytes exactly as committed, because what they
# test IS their byte content: if git were allowed to normalize them, the test
# suite would pass on the machine that wrote them and fail everywhere else.
#
# The repository is also pure ASCII apart from one marked fixture, and CI
# enforces that with a byte-level check. Git Bash's grep strips CR in text
# mode, so a CRLF file can look ASCII-clean locally and then match on a Linux
# runner; pinning LF here removes that whole class of false green.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Deliberate CRLF line endings: this fixture exists to prove the BibTeX
# parser handles CRLF without shifting its reported line numbers. Keep the
# bytes verbatim.
tests/fixtures/bib/messy.bib -text

# The only non-ASCII file in the repository: raw UTF-8 accented, CJK and
# Cyrillic author names, which is the point of it. Keep the bytes verbatim.
tests/fixtures/bib/unicode_names.bib -text

# Recorded API responses. Treated as data, not source: they are regenerated
# by tools/record_fixtures.py, never hand-edited.
tests/fixtures/cache/*.json -text -diff

*.py   text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.cff  text eol=lf
*.txt  text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
